# build output
/bin/
/dist/
# Anchored with a leading slash: this is the compiled binary at the repo root.
# Unanchored, "hooklens" matches any file OR DIRECTORY of that name at any
# depth -- which silently excluded cmd/hooklens/, so the entire entrypoint was
# never committed. Everything still built locally, because the files were on
# disk; CI cloned the repo and found no main package.
/hooklens
/hooklens.exe

# local environment
.env
.env.local

# editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# frontend (Phase 2)
node_modules/
web/dist/

# Frontend build output. Generated by `npm run build` in web/, embedded into the
# binary by internal/webui. Not committed -- it is derived, it churns on every
# build, and a stale committed copy is worse than an absent one.
#
# .gitkeep IS committed, and is load-bearing: //go:embed all:dist fails to
# COMPILE if the directory has no files at all, so a fresh clone would not build
# until someone ran npm. webui.Available() turns the resulting empty build into
# a clear message rather than a blank page.
/internal/webui/dist/*
!/internal/webui/dist/.gitkeep
